Chapter: UefiGopKeysTest
  cites Works chapter UefiConsole
  cites Works chapter GopAhci
  cites UI chapter KeyInput
  cites Foreword chapter Maybe
  cites Foreword chapter Console

 With the GOP grid on, the Dev Console's key poll reads the key ring and
 never the firmware. The scancode rows feed Set-1 codes through
 ugc-key-feed: 30 then its break 158 must read back one 'a', and 42, 30
 must read an 'A'. The stall row holds the reader while 40 keys are pushed
 into a ring of 32: the drop count must say 8, and the reader must then get
 exactly 1 through 32 in order and then nothing.

Section: Reading

  take : Integer -> Integer
  take (dummy) =
    when uefi-con-poll-key
      is None -> 0
      is Just (k) -> k.char-code

  push-n : Integer, Integer -> Integer
  push-n (i) (n) =
    if i > n then 0
    else let p = ugc-key-push i
    in push-n (i + 1) n

  drain : Integer, Integer, Integer -> Text
  drain (expect) (ok) (acc) =
    let k = take 0
    in if k == 0 then "read " & show acc & ", in order " & show ok
    else drain (expect + 1) (if k == expect then ok + 1 else ok) (acc + 1)

Section: Entry

  opening : [Console] Nothing
  opening = act
    let fb = alloc-zeroed (640 * 400 * 4) 64
    in let e = ugc-enable fb 640 400 640
    in let empty = take 0
    in let a = ugc-key-feed 30
    in let b = ugc-key-feed 158
    in let got-a = take 0
    in let s1 = ugc-key-feed 42
    in let s2 = ugc-key-feed 30
    in let got-sa = take 0
    in let s3 = ugc-key-feed 170
    in let after = take 0
    in act
      print-line-uni ("empty ring answers " & show empty)
      print-line-uni ("a: " & (if got-a == char-code (char-at "a" 0) then "a" else "code " & show got-a) & ", shift a: " & (if got-sa == char-code (char-at "A" 0) then "A" else "code " & show got-sa) & ", then " & show after)
      let p = push-n 1 40
      in print-line-uni ("stalled reader, 40 pushed into 32: drops " & show (ugc-drops 0) & ", " & drain 1 0 0)
    end
  end
